title: Star Blizzard RedFlick Scheduled Task Installation
id: 70a2af5b-b4df-4985-9d3a-77deb6839f1a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects process command lines that create or query the scheduled task
    names installed by the Star Blizzard RedFlick infection chain to stage
    and run the CosmicPulse Python backdoor (Microsoft Threat Intelligence,
    September 2026): "Internet Quality Test Connection" (collects host and
    user name, can run a remote DLL), "Network Configuration Manager"
    (prepares WebDAV for remote file-style paths) and "System Health
    Monitor" (launches control.exe), plus the SecureDNSObserver task
    documented in the earlier Ukraine Recovery Conference lure chain.
    RedFlick is delivered by a password-protected ZIP/RAR containing a VHDX
    and an LNK disguised as a PDF after a single user interaction.
references:
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/09/29/star-blizzard-refines-phishing-and-malware-delivery-with-the-redflick-technique/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/russian-state-hackers-use-new-redflick-technique-to-push-malware/
    - https://dslua.org/publications/spearphishing-via-fake-urc-2026-invitations-targets-ukrainian-csos/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/02
tags:
    - attack.t1566
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1053
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_process:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\schtasks.exe'
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
            - '\cmd.exe'
    selection_taskname:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'Internet Quality Test Connection'
            - 'Network Configuration Manager'
            - 'System Health Monitor'
            - 'SecureDNSObserver'
    condition: selection_process and selection_taskname
falsepositives:
    - Enterprise maintenance tooling that registers tasks with these generic names
    - Administrators querying or troubleshooting the same task names
level: medium
---
title: Star Blizzard RedFlick Infrastructure Beaconing
id: b4a27d1e-0c39-47a6-9d10-2e5f5c8a91d7
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects network connections to infrastructure documented for the Star
    Blizzard RedFlick chain: C2 address 103.245.213.217 reported by
    Microsoft Threat Intelligence, WebDAV delivery host 89.125.66.183 and
    remote command source 103.160.59.97 from the earlier Ukraine Recovery
    Conference lure chain, and the secure-dns-hub.com remote command domain.
references:
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/09/29/star-blizzard-refines-phishing-and-malware-delivery-with-the-redflick-technique/
    - https://dslua.org/publications/spearphishing-via-fake-urc-2026-invitations-targets-ukrainian-csos/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/02
tags:
    - attack.t1566
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_ip:
        DestinationIp:
            - 103.245.213.217
            - 89.125.66.183
            - 103.160.59.97
    selection_host:
        DestinationHostname|endswith: 'secure-dns-hub.com'
    condition: 1 of selection_*
falsepositives:
    - None known; the addresses and domain are documented Star Blizzard infrastructure
level: high
